{% extends "layout.njk" %}
{% block content %}
{% if deleted %}
  <div class="flash flash-success" role="status">Your account and all its data were deleted. Thanks for trying {{ brand }}.</div>
{% endif %}

<section class="hero">
  <h1>Accessibility reports your clients can actually read — with your logo on them.</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    {{ brand }} scans the websites you build and maintain for WCAG accessibility issues,
    watches them for regressions, and turns the findings into a plain-English, client-ready
    report. Built for freelance web designers, developers, and small agencies.
  </p>
  <div class="hero-ctas">
    <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/signup">Start your free 7-day trial</a>
    <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="#how">See how it works</a>
  </div>
  <p class="trust-line">No credit card required for the trial. Cancel anytime, refund-first policy.</p>
</section>

<section id="why">
  <h2 class="section-title">Your clients are asking about accessibility. Now you have an answer.</h2>
  <div class="grid-3">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>The pressure is real</h3>
      <p>The European Accessibility Act has been enforceable since June 2025, and US ADA web
      lawsuits continue year after year. When a client asks "are we exposed?", "let me check"
      isn't a great answer.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>The report is the product</h3>
      <p>Every scan produces a prioritized, plain-English report with your agency's name,
      logo, and colors — ready to send as-is, or to anchor a paid audit and remediation
      project.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Monitoring, not homework</h3>
      <p>Sites regress: a new plugin, a new banner, a rushed edit. {{ brand }} rescans on a
      weekly or monthly schedule and emails you when new issues appear — before the client
      notices.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="how">
  <h2 class="section-title">How it works</h2>
  <div class="grid-3">
    <div class="card"><h3>1 · Add a site</h3><p>Paste the URL. {{ brand }} discovers pages via the sitemap and internal links, then checks each one against WCAG 2.1 A/AA rules using the industry-standard axe-core engine — the same checks used by professional auditors' tooling.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>2 · Get the report</h3><p>Issues arrive grouped by severity with what's wrong, why it matters, and how to fix it — written for humans, not lawyers. Export a branded PDF or share a private link.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>3 · Stay clean</h3><p>Turn on weekly monitoring. Each scan is compared with the last one, so you see exactly what's new, what's fixed, and what's still open.</p></div>
  </div>

  <div class="honesty">
    <strong>An honest note about automated scanning.</strong> Automated checks reliably find
    roughly a third of WCAG issues — the mechanical ones like missing alt text, broken labels,
    and low contrast. No tool can certify a site as "compliant," and anyone who says otherwise
    is selling something. {{ brand }} finds the issues a machine can find, tracks them over
    time, and tells you plainly where human review is still needed. Your reports say the same,
    which is exactly why clients trust them.
  </div>
</section>

<section id="pricing">
  <h2 class="section-title">Simple, flat pricing</h2>
  <div class="grid-3">
    <div class="card pricing-card">
      <h3>Free trial</h3>
      <p class="pricing-price">$0<small> / 7 days</small></p>
      <ul class="pricing-features">
        <li>Everything in Solo</li>
        <li>No credit card required</li>
        <li>Your data is kept if you upgrade later</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/signup">Start free</a>
    </div>
    <div class="card pricing-card">
      <h3>Solo</h3>
      <p class="pricing-price">$29<small> / month</small></p>
      <ul class="pricing-features">
        <li>10 sites</li>
        <li>25 pages per scan</li>
        <li>Weekly or monthly monitoring</li>
        <li>White-label PDF reports</li>
        <li>Share links for clients</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/signup">Start with a free trial</a>
    </div>
    <div class="card pricing-card">
      <h3>Studio</h3>
      <p class="pricing-price">$59<small> / month</small></p>
      <ul class="pricing-features">
        <li>30 sites</li>
        <li>100 pages per scan</li>
        <li>Weekly or monthly monitoring</li>
        <li>White-label PDF reports</li>
        <li>Share links for clients</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/signup">Start with a free trial</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="muted" style="text-align:center">Flat price. No per-page metering surprises, no per-seat fees, no annual contract. Cancel in two clicks.</p>
</section>

<section id="faq">
  <h2 class="section-title">Questions, answered plainly</h2>
  <div class="faq-item">
    <h3>Will this make my client's site "ADA compliant" or "EAA compliant"?</h3>
    <p>No tool can promise that, including this one. Compliance is a legal judgment about the
    whole experience; automated checks cover the detectable subset of WCAG (roughly a third of
    issues). {{ brand }} finds those, documents them, and monitors regressions — genuinely
    useful evidence of effort, not a certificate. For high-risk clients, pair it with a manual
    audit by an accessibility specialist.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="faq-item">
    <h3>How is this different from the accessibility overlay widgets?</h3>
    <p>Overlays inject a script that tries to patch symptoms in the visitor's browser; they've
    been widely criticized by accessibility experts, and the FTC fined one major vendor $1M for
    deceptive compliance claims. {{ brand }} takes the opposite approach: it tells you what to
    fix in the actual site, so the fix is real and permanent.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="faq-item">
    <h3>What exactly does a scan check?</h3>
    <p>Each page is loaded in a real browser and checked against the WCAG 2.1 A/AA rule set of
    axe-core, the open-source engine used by most professional accessibility tooling —
    contrast, alt text, form labels, landmarks, ARIA validity, keyboard traps detectable in
    markup, and more.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="faq-item">
    <h3>Can it scan pages behind a login?</h3>
    <p>Not yet. {{ brand }} scans publicly reachable pages. Login-protected scanning is on the
    roadmap; tell us if you need it and we'll prioritize accordingly.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="faq-item">
    <h3>Why did my scan find fewer pages than my site has?</h3>
    <p>Scans are capped by plan (25 pages on Solo, 100 on Studio) and discover pages from your
    sitemap and internal links. If key pages are missing, check they're linked or in your
    sitemap.xml. Caps keep scans fast and pricing flat.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="faq-item">
    <h3>What happens when my site is behind bot protection?</h3>
    <p>Some firewalls block automated visitors. The report will say so honestly, page by page,
    instead of inventing results. Since you build the site, allowlisting our user agent
    (<code>SiteRampBot</code>) usually solves it in minutes.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="faq-item">
    <h3>What's your refund policy?</h3>
    <p>If {{ brand }} didn't work for you, email us within 30 days of any charge and we refund
    it. No forms, no interrogation.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="faq-item">
    <h3>Do you store my clients' data?</h3>
    <p>Only what a scan produces: page URLs, detected issues, and HTML snippets of the flagged
    elements from public pages. No visitor data, no analytics beacons, nothing injected into
    the sites. Delete a site (or your account) and its data is gone immediately.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="text-align:center; margin-top:3rem">
  <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/signup">Start your free 7-day trial</a>
</section>
{% endblock %}
